# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts ActiveMQ (`activemq start` daemonizes), waits for the
# web console on 8161 to answer, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING with the unauthenticated /api/ (Jolokia+REST)
#     endpoint exposed when the agent starts (the vulnerability is live);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, not the broker, so restarting the broker cannot
#     kill the container.
#
# The remediation edits conf/jetty.xml to require authentication on /api/* and
# then RESTARTS the broker to load it. There IS a "forgot to restart" case here:
# editing jetty.xml without restarting leaves the running broker still serving
# /api/ unauthenticated, which the behavioural check detects (still 200 -> FAIL).
